  "response": "## The finding\n\n`crime_00071` — **Duplicate Component Shape** (medium, confidence 0.7), shape hash `e96b55b64336…`, 4 files / 4 occurrences:\n\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |\n\nI read all four subtrees. They are byte-identical except for one token — the submit button's text (`Create Invoice` vs `Edit Invoice`). The cancel `href`, the 11-class utility string on the `Link`, `mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4`, and `<Button type=\"submit\">` are the same in every copy:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link\n    href=\"/dashboard/invoices\"\n    className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n  >\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nThat's the drift risk in concrete terms: a hover state, a focus ring, an `aria-disabled` pending state, or a spacing change has to be hand-applied in four places, and nothing fails if you only do three.\n\n## The scope caveat, up front\n\n`dashboard/final-example` and `dashboard/starter-example` are **separate Next.js apps** — each has its own `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, and `@/app/*` path alias, and neither imports from the other. So this is *not* one shared component across four call sites; it's **one component per app, two call sites each**. Consolidating across the app boundary would require a workspace package that doesn't exist here (and would defeat the starter/final teaching split). The starter and final copies are expected to diverge over the tutorial's lifetime.\n\n## Proposed component\n\nTwo new files, same content, one per app:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`\n\nIt sits next to `app/ui/button.tsx` rather than under `app/ui/invoices/` — the footer isn't invoice-specific, and `login-form.tsx` is a plausible second consumer.\n\n```tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\n\ninterface FormActionsProps {\n  /** Destination for the cancel link — e.g. \"/dashboard/invoices\". */\n  cancelHref: string;\n  /** Submit button contents. The only thing that differs across today's call sites. */\n  submitLabel: React.ReactNode;\n  /** Cancel link contents. */\n  cancelLabel?: React.ReactNode;\n  /** Slot: extra actions rendered before Cancel (Delete, Save draft, …). */\n  children?: React.ReactNode;\n}\n\nexport function FormActions({\n  cancelHref,\n  submitLabel,\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  children,\n}: FormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      {children}\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\">{submitLabel}</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Public API**\n\n| Member | Type | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cancelHref` | `string` | yes | Required rather than defaulted to `/dashboard/invoices` — a default would silently send a login form to the invoices list. |\n| `submitLabel` | `React.ReactNode` | yes | `ReactNode`, not `string`, so a caller can pass `<>Save <Spinner/></>`. |\n| `cancelLabel` | `React.ReactNode` | no, `'Cancel'` | The one value that is stable today; defaulted so call sites stay two lines. |\n| `children` | `React.ReactNode` | no | The only slot. Leading-actions position, before Cancel. |\n\nDeliberately **not** in the API: `className`, `submitProps`, or a `justify` prop. Each is a hole through which the four copies re-diverge — a caller passing `className=\"justify-between\"` gets an untracked variant, which is the problem we're removing. Add them when a second layout genuinely exists.\n\nThe component needs no `'use client'` directive; `Link` and `button` work in either environment, and the four call-site files already carry the directive.\n\n## Files that would change\n\n**New (2):**\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`\n\n**Edited (4):**\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` — replace 142–150; drop the `Link`/`Button` imports if unused elsewhere in the file\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` — replace 152–160, same import cleanup\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` — replace 101–109\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` — replace 112–120\n\nEach call site collapses to:\n\n```tsx\n<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\" />\n```\n\nCheck the `Link` and `Button` imports individually per file before deleting them — `edit-form.tsx` in particular may use `Button` elsewhere; a repo-wide import strip would break the build.\n\n## What this does and doesn't fix\n\nIt closes `crime_00071` and removes ~36 lines. It does **not** touch the adjacent findings in the same files, which need separate work: `crime_00074`/`00075`/`00078`/`00079` (design token escapes — the `px 18px` literals live in the fieldset above, not in this subtree) and `crime_00072`/`00073` (the `\"paid\"`/`\"pending\"` checks duplicated across the forms and `status.tsx`, which want a policy function, not a component).",
